 ## Background
-The Generic Operators family originates from the field of "imaging transforms" for visualizing surfaces and volumes, specifically in the context of robust structure rendering [S1]. The terminology and specific operators ($I_r, I_l, I_b, I_e, S_b, B, B', C, R_{n_c}, R_{n_e}, F, G$) are defined in the foundational paper on imaging transforms [S1]. The methods were developed to address artifacts in volume rendering, such as slicing artifacts, by using shape-based interpolation and precise boundary detection [S1]. The family is particularly relevant for rendering robust structures where high-quality surface approximation is required, often outperforming standard grey-volume rendering techniques [S1].
